We present a novel method for simulating modified gravity theories, specifically those with conformal coupling, using a full N-body approach. This method is based on the Einstein-Boltzmann code, which has been adapted to accommodate a wide range of modified gravity theories. Our approach is particularly well-suited for simulating the growth of structure in the universe, and we demonstrate its effectiveness by applying it to a modified gravity model that exhibits a significant enhancement in the growth rate of structure. We also discuss the implications of our findings for the detection of modified gravity in future surveys. Our code is publicly available for download. 

